        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daragh O'Malley, Bob Hoskins, Helen Mirren, Sean Bean, Assumpta Serna, Martin Glyn Murray\n- Works: The Long Good Friday, Withnail and I, Sharpe's Rifles, Sharpe, Tales of the Unexpected, Waking the Dead, Wire in the Blood, Silent Witness, Vera, Longitude, Cleopatra, The Magnificent Seven, Vendetta, Camelot, Shaughnessy, Families, The Bill, Aristocrats, Enigma, Enemy at the Gates, Captain Corelli's Mandolin, Made in Estonia, Heartbeat\n- Organizations: ITV, ABC, CBS\n\nFacts:\n- The Long Good Friday is a British gangster film starring Bob Hoskins and Helen Mirren.\n- Sharpe's Rifles was shown on ITV in 1993 and stars Sean Bean, Daragh O'Malley, and Assumpta Serna.\n- Daragh O'Malley first appeared in roles in the films The Long Good Friday and Withnail and I.\n- Daragh O'Malley had leading guest roles in the UK television series Tales of the Unexpected, Waking the Dead, Wire in the Blood, Silent Witness, and Vera.\n- Daragh O'Malley also appeared in Longitude, Cleopatra for ABC, The Magnificent Seven for CBS, and the US TV films Vendetta, Camelot, and Shaughnessy.\n- Martin Glyn Murray was born on 1 February 1966 in Helsingør, Denmark, and is a Danish-born British actor.\n- Martin Glyn Murray played Mark Thompson in Families and has also appeared in The Bill, Sharpe, Aristocrats, Enigma, Enemy at the Gates, Captain Corelli's Mandolin, Made in Estonia, and Heartbeat.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
